<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<SmellBaseline>
  <ManuallySuppressedIssues>
    <!--
      `src/debug` was added to detekt's source list on 2026-10-05 (issue #99,
      openspec/changes/androidapp-debug-lint-policy). Linting it surfaced 15
      findings, all in DebugSeedActivity.kt: 9 were real formatting defects and
      were auto-corrected, and the 4 below are the tool doing its job.

      They live in ManuallySuppressedIssues rather than CurrentIssues on purpose.
      A CurrentIssues entry is regenerated from a run and quietly absorbs whatever
      the next run finds, so a genuinely new defect in this file would join these
      four and become indistinguishable from them. These are written by hand, which
      means a fifth has to be a decision.

      Each reason is about what this tool *is*, not about debug code in general. A
      justification written as "this is debug code" would be the blanket exemption
      wearing a suppression's syntax, and it would be copy-pasted into production
      where it is not true.
    -->

    <!--
      A seeder is invoked from a deep link and must finish before the app it seeds
      draws anything. There is no composition to inject a scope into and no caller
      to hand a dispatcher to: the activity is the whole lifecycle. Making this
      async would mean the process could be backgrounded, or the deep link followed
      again, with the database half-written. So it blocks, on purpose, for a seeder
      the developer is watching.
    -->
    <ID>NoRunBlocking:DebugSeedActivity.kt:DebugSeedActivity$runBlocking { seed(params) }</ID>

    <!--
      Seed rows are stamped with the developer's real wall clock, and a scenario
      asserting on "today" has to see the same "today" the app computes. There is no
      Clock in the graph a deep link can reach, and injecting a fake here would make
      seeded data disagree with the running app rather than agree with it. This is
      the one place reading the system clock is the correct behaviour, which is why
      it is baselined individually instead of exempted by source set.
    -->
    <ID>NoDirectClockSystem:DebugSeedActivity.kt:DebugSeedActivity$Clock.System</ID>

    <!--
      `resolveDate` resolves a seed's "today" anchor, so it reads the same clock for
      the same reason as the stamping above. One entry covers all four call sites:
      detekt keys the signature on the expression, not the line.
    -->
    <ID>NoDirectClockSystem:DebugSeedActivity.kt:resolveDate$Clock.System</ID>

    <!--
      A seeding tool that throws takes the developer's app down with it, and the
      exception the repository layer throws is not this module's to enumerate — the
      same reason SupabaseSyncApiClient's transport catch is baselined in
      baseline-shared.xml. The failure is logged with its cause and the activity
      still finishes, so a partial seed shows up in logcat instead of as a crash
      dialog over an empty database.
    -->
    <ID>TooGenericExceptionCaught:DebugSeedActivity.kt:DebugSeedActivity$e: Throwable</ID>
  </ManuallySuppressedIssues>
  <CurrentIssues>
  </CurrentIssues>
</SmellBaseline>
